From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Commit the diagnostic log to disk from the queue trace

Windows 95 does not update a file's size in the directory until the file is
closed, and its write-behind cache holds the sectors meanwhile. The crash filter
works around this by calling fclose(stderr) before it writes -- but a program
that HANGS never reaches any handler, so it leaves a log of zero bytes no matter
how much it wrote.

That cost an hour today. A run was inspected mid-flight, DKRR.LOG read zero
bytes, and the obvious reading -- "the program produced nothing, so it stopped
early" -- was wrong twice over: the trace was not even enabled in that launch,
and the program was running normally. Two opposite diagnoses behind one
observation, which is the worst kind.

dkr_diag_commit (defined in the game, declared weak here so the witness binaries
that link ultramodern without it still link) calls _commit, which is
FlushFileBuffers -- it forces both the cache and the directory entry. Called from
the periodic queue-total trace, it makes the log readable while the program is
still running.

This is what turned the DP-edge fix from plausible into checked: the run could be
read at 570 display lists, then again at 1135, without stopping it.

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
--- a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@
 #include "ultramodern/ultra64.h"
 #include "ultramodern/ultramodern.hpp"
 
+// Defined by the game (game_main.cpp): flushes the log AND updates the directory
+// entry. Declared weak so that the trial binaries, which link ultramodern without
+// the game, still link.
+extern "C" void dkr_diag_commit(void) __attribute__((weak));
+
 struct MessageDeliveryState {
     ultramodern::mutex mutex;
     ultramodern::condition_variable condition;
@@ -336,6 +341,12 @@
                                  "[trace][mq] total msg=0x%08X deposited=%u refused=%u requeued=%u\n",
                                  seen[m][0], tot[m][0], tot[m][1], tot[m][2]);
                 }
+                // Force the log onto the disk: Windows 95 only updates the size
+                // at close time, so a frozen program leaves a zero-byte file
+                // whatever it wrote. Without this call, "the program stopped
+                // early" and "the program is still running" give the same
+                // observation.
+                if (dkr_diag_commit) { dkr_diag_commit(); }
             }
         }
         if (!sent && to_send.requeue_if_blocked) {
